# test: bare_help
# description: Bare amux without a real TTY prints top-level help (on a TTY it
# opens the fleet TUI; scripts and pipes get help, never an alt-screen)

## Environment

terminal:
  name: T1

## Test

@T1
> amux
Terminal multiplexer for AI agents (Claude, Codex, etc.)

Usage: amux [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ui      Open the fleet TUI (the default when run with no command)
  new     Create a new agent session
  attach  Attach to an existing agent session
  rm      Remove an agent session by exact name or UUID
  list    List running agent sessions, folding child agents into their parent
  server  Manage the amux server lifecycle
  init    Initialize amux (cloud mode, authentication)
  pair    Pair this device with another amux daemon
  peer    Show trusted peers
  unpair  Remove trust for a peer
  update  Update amux to the latest version
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>  Path to config file (YAML format). Also read from `AMUX_CONFIG`, so managed Claude hooks and daemons spawned by a wrapper find the same instance without adding a config flag to their command [env: AMUX_CONFIG=]
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version
